 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Polygon-based Cropping](11787-polygon-based-cropping.md)
-Supports arbitrary convex or non-convex polygonal shapes in screen space, unlike the axis-aligned planar cuts of this method. Choose when free-form region selection is required.
+Polygon-based cropping is a voxel-wise volume rendering technique that masks voxels based on a user-defined 2D polygon drawn in the display (screen) coordinate space. It solves the problem of interactive, free-form region-of-interest selection by converting screen-space constraints into volume-space visibility masks. It differs from planar clipping methods by supporting arbitrary convex or non-convex polygonal shapes rather than just axis-aligned or arbitrary planar cuts, and it operates by explicitly iterating over voxels to test their projected positions against the polygon boundary.
+
+### Interactive Cropping
+Interactive cropping enables real-time adjustment of the volume along X, Y, and Z axes using keyboard controls [S3, unofficial]. Cropping is toggled on/off by pressing 'C' or 'c' [S3, unofficial]. The X-axis is adjusted with Left/Right Arrow keys, the Y-axis with Up/Down Arrow keys, and the Z-axis with PageUp/PageDown keys [S3, unofficial]. Holding Shift while pressing arrow keys expands the crop region [S3, unofficial]. Pressing 'R' resets the crop to the full volume bounds [S3, unofficial]. The crop planes are initialized at full bounds using `vtk.vtkPlanes` and `vtk.vtkPoints` with 8 corner points [S3, unofficial]. Physical coordinates for crop planes are calculated from normalized ranges and volume bounds, then passed to the mapper via `SetCroppingRegionPlanes` [S3, unofficial]. A minimum crop width of 0.1 must be enforced to prevent degenerate planes [S3, unofficial].
 
